From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: add silent diagnostic counters for the offload path

IPv6 flows never bind to the PPE: the engine learns matching UNBIND
5-tuple entries with the exact layout our builder produces (verified on
hardware via devmem), the staged rules get [HW_OFFLOAD], yet bind stays
flat while IPv4 binds fine. The old bring-up instrumentation was printk
based and has been removed; this adds a zero-cost, printk-free
replacement to pin down where the v6 chain stops:

- per-stage rx-commit counters, v4/v6 split for lookup-miss / no-slot /
  bound,
- per-reason accept/reject counters in flow replace, v4/v6 split for
  accepts,
- an RX crsn histogram (counter only),

all dumped by the new debugfs file econet_ppe/diag. No behavioural
change.
